        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e76a793f-c938-3815-bca8-6ba96ec1a2bc",
                "word": "торопливо",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "77fa0f9c-5d75-3ba1-8e4d-a6d77dd442a3",
                        "entry_id": "e76a793f-c938-3815-bca8-6ba96ec1a2bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "очень быстро, с поспешностью"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db33102d-02a7-4ca3-8935-34f3f1a34f1d",
                                "sense_id": "77fa0f9c-5d75-3ba1-8e4d-a6d77dd442a3",
                                "text": "На перевозе ночевало много народу, и уже одна большая завозня, битком набитая лошадьми и телегами с приподнятыми передками и торчащими вверх оглоблями, чернелась на середине Волги, а другая торопливо грузилась, чтобы воспользоваться благополучным временем."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93ed9c4c-188f-451c-b6e6-d53b3e1e3e46",
                        "source_entry_id": "e76a793f-c938-3815-bca8-6ba96ec1a2bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "77fa0f9c-5d75-3ba1-8e4d-a6d77dd442a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "hurriedly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hurriedly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                        "entry_id": "c78db753-cd52-3560-8cd0-c159f45d93af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a hurried manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56177ffe-cfad-4ab0-9d3b-1b11ea7234c9",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                                "text": "The mother, Ekaterina Pavlovna, who at one time had been handsome, but now, asthmatic, depressed, vague, and over-feeble for her years, tried to entertain me with conversation about painting. Having heard from her daughter that I might come to Shelkovka, she had hurriedly recalled two or three of my landscapes which she had seen in exhibitions in Moscow, and now asked what I meant to express by them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b4f372b-0a25-403d-94ac-38798c65fc2f",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                                "text": "“In a moment, he has torn the letter into long thin strips, and rolling them up into spills he thrusts them hurriedly in amongst the other spills in the vase on the mantle-piece.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c371a5f5-9966-465d-b8d6-242baf42a040",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                                "text": "If the kind of network we envisage is to be established, it would be unwise to begin any of its services hurriedly with older stock, which, however admirable in its day, now has an air of faded Edwardian splendour that is out of joint with the times."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d834ac0-2e4e-4791-98d1-57e9639ad495",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                                "text": "But Johnson [...] hurriedly [c]hanged his plea to guilty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dc177aa-e99f-4982-9dbb-6815791ccc96",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac24c1d-3519-3e69-84f6-199ddc984cc7",
                                                "text": "The result was that trains ran as normal on November 7 and 9, although there was still disruption on Saturday November 5, owing to the short notice as rosters were hurriedly rewritten. Rosters are typically agreed a week in advance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "be4ac7e4-bfd4-4406-b8b4-d74d023b9dab",
                        "source_entry_id": "e76a793f-c938-3815-bca8-6ba96ec1a2bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "77fa0f9c-5d75-3ba1-8e4d-a6d77dd442a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "hastily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hastily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db1c7dab-9d93-3be4-8ace-c3770ae32762",
                                        "entry_id": "9a743cdd-1b40-3322-94be-566372b790ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a hasty manner; quickly or hurriedly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46eaceea-523e-4a0c-985a-dff394daa9b9",
                                                "sense_id": "db1c7dab-9d93-3be4-8ace-c3770ae32762",
                                                "text": "The departure was not unduly prolonged.[…]Within the door Mrs. Spoker hastily imparted to Mrs. Love a few final sentiments on the subject of Divine Intention in the disposition of buckets; farewells and last commiserations; a deep, guttural instigation to the horse; and the wheels of the waggonette crunched heavily away into obscurity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99579e44-1e6f-4eb4-8591-88253bb90475",
                                                "sense_id": "db1c7dab-9d93-3be4-8ace-c3770ae32762",
                                                "text": "The last occasion on which the Kaiser [Wilhelm II] used this train was for an inglorious journey into Holland towards the end of the 1914 war. He spent the night in it at Eysden [Eijsden], while the Queen of the Netherlands and a hastily summoned Cabinet debated what to do with him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "956737a4-882c-4062-b3e1-0d597a61d10d",
                                                "sense_id": "db1c7dab-9d93-3be4-8ace-c3770ae32762",
                                                "text": "Eudemis moved hastily but as unobtrusively as he could through the gaping crowd[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f844bc29-3eee-367c-ba37-0c294f793050",
                                        "entry_id": "9a743cdd-1b40-3322-94be-566372b790ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Soon, shortly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0256fa2c-def6-4f68-a5ef-0c231fd06937",
                                                "sense_id": "f844bc29-3eee-367c-ba37-0c294f793050",
                                                "text": "she with liquors strong his eyes did steepe, / That nothing should him hastily awake [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00de7a1d-9f0f-4ffd-a396-c9c2a03b9480",
                        "source_entry_id": "e76a793f-c938-3815-bca8-6ba96ec1a2bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "77fa0f9c-5d75-3ba1-8e4d-a6d77dd442a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "in haste",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "in haste",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "056eaeb8-a428-30c8-9375-7c7a5e4ea6ee",
                                        "entry_id": "c613b420-53a7-391b-8fd0-2546de6951b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a hurry, hastily, quickly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ccfe33b-1711-4e13-8769-6fc599849d8b",
                                                "sense_id": "056eaeb8-a428-30c8-9375-7c7a5e4ea6ee",
                                                "text": "In her haste to get to school, she almost forgot her school bag."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0881ef81-5af5-3de0-889b-03437e4b6819",
                                        "entry_id": "c613b420-53a7-391b-8fd0-2546de6951b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Too quickly, without careful thought and planning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e824b4af-0fce-487a-bbdf-3d966c3ef63b",
                                                "sense_id": "0881ef81-5af5-3de0-889b-03437e4b6819",
                                                "text": "The decision had been taken in haste, and hence was the bad outcome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
